# The mesh sidecar's compiled Go libraries (scripts/build-mesh-mobile.sh). CI
# rebuilds them for every release and the bytes are not guaranteed to repeat,
# so hashing them would give every release a new runtime version and no
# over-the-air update would ever match an installed app. The Go sources in
# modules/pokket-mesh/go are fingerprinted instead: they decide the build.
modules/pokket-mesh/android/libs/**/*
modules/pokket-mesh/android/src/main/jniLibs/**/*
modules/pokket-mesh/ios/Meshmobile.xcframework/**/*

# Tests of the Go sources change nothing that ships.
modules/pokket-mesh/go/**/*_test.go

# react-native-webgpu's podspec copies Dawn's xcframework into its own package
# directory at `pod install` (libs/apple), so the fingerprint taken before a
# build and the one the build takes after installing pods would differ, and the
# iOS build fails with "runtime version mismatch". The copy is
# react-native-webgpu-dawn's, whose version react-native-webgpu's package.json
# (fingerprinted) pins.
node_modules/react-native-webgpu/libs/**/*
